WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.634
-Welcome back. Taylor Swift
is here! Come on!

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:07.133
"Red" is out right now,
actually.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:09.300
It's officially coming out
right now while this airing.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.601
-Oh. Yeah, I think it's out.

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:14.200
-Your fans are amazing fans.
I will just say that.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.634
I know you said it earlier, but
they obviously are so excited

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:19.033
that you're here on our show,

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:21.534
so we're getting a lot of buzz
from your fans.

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:23.467
And they were like, "Wait. What
are they going to talk about?

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:26.701
What's going on? I heard this.
[ Blabbering ]

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:28.200
This is ten seconds long."

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.234
There's Easter eggs that maybe
aren't even really Easter eggs.

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:34.000
-Yeah, it's sort of a tradition

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.534
that we started
a very long time ago.

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:38.234
I think the first time
that I started dropping

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:41.667
sort of cryptic clues
and things in my music

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:46.534
is when I was 14 and 15
putting together my first album.

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:48.701
And I wanted to put --
I wanted to do something

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:51.834
that incentivized fans
to read the lyrics

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:53.801
because my lyrics are what
I'm most proud of

00:00:53.801 --> 00:00:56.000
out of everything that I do,
every aspect of my job,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.367
so I really wanted people
to read the lyrics.

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:01.534
And, um, when I was a kid,
I used to leaf through

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:04.367
CD booklets and just read
the teeny, tiny print

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.000
and just obsess over it.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.767
And so I wanted
to incentivize them.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:12.200
So in my lyrics, for my first,
you know, several albums,

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.300
I would have all
lower-case-letter lyrics,

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.300
except for capital letter,

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.634
capital letter, capital letter
every once in a while.

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:20.968
And if they circled
the capital letter,

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:24.667
and wrote them down,
it spelled out a secret code,

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:25.868
a secret passage.

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:28.167
-That's so fun.
-It was really --

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:30.000
it was really fun,
and it would either tell them

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.467
a story about the album

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:34.200
or a hint about
what the song was about.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.667
And so that's when it started.

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:38.100
But when it got out of control
was...

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.901
-[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:42.067
-Was when I started to realize
that it wasn't just me

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:44.701
that had fun with this,
that they had fun with it, too.

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:46.033
-Oh, yeah.
-And I should never

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.934
have learned that
because then I couldn't stop.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:52.334
And then all I started thinking
of was how do I hint at things?

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.901
Like, how far
is too far in advance?

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:57.767
Can I hint at something
three years in advance?

00:01:57.767 --> 00:02:00.067
Can I even plan things out
that far?

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:01.767
I think I'm gonna try to do it.

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:04.033
The first time that we did
a crazy video like that

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.133
was a video called
"Look What You Made Me Do,"

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:09.200
and I started playing
with doing nods

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.634
to former musical eras
I've been in, in my career

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:14.968
and all kinds of weird stuff

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.100
for them to just go through
the video and be like,

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.834
"That over there! What's that?
What's that? What's that?

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:22.234
Does this connect to that?
What does that mean?"

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:24.667
-I do that.
-Really?

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:26.834
-Yes! I did that
with "Folklore."

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:28.934
I go, "Wait. What? Betty? What?"

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:30.300
-There's a lot.
There's a lot going --

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.400
There's, like,
a fictional love triangle

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.834
between three
fictional teenagers

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:36.467
in the "Folklore" album.
-I know all about it.

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:39.367
-There's all kinds of, like,
really, really --

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:41.767
-Yeah, we go really
into the weeds over it.

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:45.200
And look. I think that it is
perfectly reasonable for people

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.033
to be normal music fans

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:50.234
and to have a normal
relationship to music.

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:53.267
But if you want to go down

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:55.667
a rabbit hole with us,
come along.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.267
-Taylor is your person.
-The water's great.

00:02:57.267 --> 00:02:59.133
-Yeah. The waters fine.
-Jump in.

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:00.434
-Yeah.
-We're all mad here.

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:02.901
-Exactly right.
-Yeah.

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:05.934
-Also, with "All Too Well,"

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:08.767
with the short film,
I noticed --

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:11.033
I noticed a ton of
Easter eggs in this.

00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:13.067
-Oh, it's ridiculous
how many there are.

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:14.467
-Whoo! It's so good.

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:17.100
I'm like, "That's a thing.
That's another thing."

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.067
I want to watch this
like 30 times.

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:20.701
-I really love that you --
-I'm geeking out.

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:22.267
-Thank you.
-I'm a uber fan. Yeah.

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:24.067
-That's so awesome.
-My daughters are so

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:25.801
into it, too,
which is, like, the best.

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:27.434
'Cause I'm like,
"Yeah, let's put in..."

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:28.901
Oh, they love you so much.

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:32.300
My little daughter, she goes,
"Dad, I have a special talent.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:34.234
I can tell whenever
it's a Taylor song."

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:35.667
-[ Gasps ]
-And I go, "You can?"

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:37.334
But she doesn't realize
that's all we play.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:38.868
-Oh, my God.

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:42.234
That's so amazing. Please
tell her I said thank you.

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:44.133
-Yeah. She loves you.
-That's so wonderful.

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:47.234
-This is a giant week.
You have "Red," right?

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:48.634
"Taylor's Version." Coming out.

00:03:48.634 --> 00:03:51.234
You have "All Too Well,"
a short film coming out.

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:52.734
-Yeah.
-You're performing

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:54.300
on "Saturday Night Live."
-Yeah.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.767
-This Saturday.
-This Saturday.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.400
-This is your fifth time
performing.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.934
I've seen you perform live --

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:00.501
By the way,
do you remember this?

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.634
This made me laugh so --
I just love you so much.

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:04.567
We were at the Time 100 event.

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:06.534
You were performing.
And you were fantastic.

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:07.968
And you played on the piano,

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:10.067
and you actually
kicked your heels off,

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:11.834
and you were just playing
and you were awesome.

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:13.868
But before that, I go, "Taylor,
what's up? Good to see you.

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.968
How are you?" And I saw Tree,
and I go, "Hey, what's up?"

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:17.868
I go,
"What are you doing tonight?"

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:20.067
And you go, "I don't know.
Probably go play pool

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:21.567
or something
if you want to hang out."

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:24.434
I go, "No, no. I meant, what
songs are you doing tonight?"

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:27.000
Like, I'm -- I'm so old.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.534
I can't hang out with you after.
I'm so old.

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.834
I just wanted to know
what songs.

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:35.934
-It is too late o'clock.
I was just seeing, how are you?

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:37.200
-Grandpa needs to go to sleep.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.901
I'm like,
"What are you doing tonight?"

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:41.300
-I was like, "I don't know!
Where's the party?!

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.634
I'll throw it! You throw it!
We can throw a joint party!"

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:48.300
-So, this Saturday.
"Saturday Night Live."

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:51.367
What two songs -- Can we hint
to what songs you're performing?

00:04:51.367 --> 00:04:53.367
-I love to hint.

00:04:53.367 --> 00:04:56.467
Um, which two songs?

00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:58.834
What if...
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:02.067
-...it was not two songs

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:05.734
as much as it was one song that
is the length of three songs?

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:07.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.467 --> 00:05:08.934
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:12.267
-I think I know exactly
what you mean by this.

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:17.167
I got it! I got it!
I know exactly --

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:20.267
I know...all too well...
what you mean, Betty.

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:23.534
Taylor Swift, everyone!
Taylor is performing

00:05:23.534 --> 00:05:26.033
on "Saturday Night Live"
this weekend.

00:05:26.033 --> 00:05:30.334
"Red (Taylor's Version)"
is officially out now!

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.334
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:33.968
Come on back, everybody!

